  "steps": [
    "Compare the live draft to the revision 8 backup and each live card to its saved before data. Stop on any mismatch.",
    "For each card, remove only the optional bodyLayout field using assets:update. The illustrated presentation remains the default. This avoids an existing conversion-validator rejection of that field.",
    "Run assets:convertTreacheryToCustom for each existing card. Run assets:update with its fitted candidate data. No replacement asset records are created.",
    "Wait for both card publications to become current, verify complete text and unchanged image proportions, and refresh the local production-card bindings.",
    "Save the candidate book through rulebooks:save with expected_revision 8. Verify the saved settings and contents.",
    "Publish through rulebooks:publish with the returned revision and confirmed true. Verify public Edition 2, HTML and PDF delivery."
  ],
  "recovery": [
    "The unchanged revision 8 Rulebook export is retained. Its contents can be saved and published as a subsequent Edition if the release must be superseded.",
    "The complete original and proposed data for both cards are retained. The old layout can be restored inside the custom cards, preserving their IDs. Type conversion has no normal UI reverse operation; restoring the treachery classification would need a separately confirmed administrative repair.",
    "Do not change owners, groups, account data, authentication, or unrelated records. Do not add or deploy a server write path. Stop if Central identity is rejected."
  ]
